From: OpenDSL build layer
Subject: [PATCH] Retire online-update actions at the native controller boundary

Review A01: appDo_rc_service ignored the exit status of the retired
/usr/script/webs_{update,upgrade}.sh helpers and still ran the service-stop,
System_Entry.upgrade_fw and commit machinery for a failed download. Retire
the actions at the controller: a nonzero guard result returns immediately,
before any service-stop, signal, upgrade-state or commit/flash action. The
guards themselves (overlays/security) write no WebCustom_Entry state,
so retirement can never poison the next manual local upload.

Recheck C04: the retired branches now return the caller's no-change result
(0) instead of the "modified/running service" value 2, so do_apply_cgi does
not emit MODIFIED/RUN SERVICE nor call tcapi_save() for a retired-only
request; mixed requests still produce their own caller-side results.

--- a/apps/public/boa-asp/src/asp/asp_handler.c
+++ b/apps/public/boa-asp/src/asp/asp_handler.c
@@ -9264,8 +9264,19 @@
 		}
 		/* [SET] [Firmware Update] download fw server info */
 		else if(!strcmp(rc_service, "start_webs_update")) {
-			eval("/usr/script/webs_update.sh");
-			app_method_hit = 2;
+			if(eval("/usr/script/webs_update.sh") == 0) {
+				app_method_hit = 2;
+			}
+			else {
+				/* OpenDSL: online updates are retired. A nonzero guard
+				   result means retirement, never success: return the
+				   caller's no-change result here, before any download,
+				   service-stop, upgrade-state or flash/commit action and
+				   before the caller's tcapi_save() path. The ordinary
+				   local upload path keeps its own native validation. */
+				_dprintf("[AiHome] appDo_rc_service: online update retired\n");
+				return 0;
+			}
 		}
 		else if(!strcmp(rc_service, "restart_wireless")) {
 			char *argv[] = { "/userfs/bin/tcapi", "commit", "WLan", NULL };
@@ -9277,7 +9288,18 @@
 		}
 		/* [SET] [General] Firmware Upgrade */
 		else if(!strcmp(rc_service, "start_webs_upgrade")) {
-			eval("/usr/script/webs_upgrade.sh");
+			if(eval("/usr/script/webs_upgrade.sh") != 0) {
+				/* OpenDSL: online downloads are retired. A nonzero guard
+				   result is retirement, not a state the next manual
+				   upload should read: return the caller's no-change
+				   result before the service-stop / upgrade-state /
+				   commit machinery below and before the caller's
+				   tcapi_save() path runs for this request. Mixed
+				   requests that contain real attribute or service
+				   changes keep their own caller-side result. */
+				_dprintf("[AiHome] appDo_rc_service: online upgrade retired\n");
+				return 0;
+			}
 			/*stop_service();*/
 			killall_tk("clean_cache.sh");
 			sleep(1);
